# DTR-COORDINATES: 

# Fix StackOverflowError in JSON parser regex

File: itr-compiler/src/main/scala/itrcompiler/infrastructure/parsers/JSONFormat.scala

Problem:
The content field regex ((?:[^"\\]|\\.)*) causes catastrophic backtracking
on large inputs. The regex engine recursive matching stack overflows.

Fix:
Replace line 20-21 regex with simpler pattern that avoids nested alternation.

Replace:
  val cuPattern =
    """\{\s*"cu-id"\s*:\s*"([^"]+)"\s*,\s*"dtr-coordinates"\s*:\s*\[([^\]]*)\]\s*,\s*"content"\s*:\s*"((?:[^"\\\\]|\\\\.)*)"\s*\}""".r

With:
  val cuPattern =
    """\{\s*"cu-id"\s*:\s*"([^"]+)"\s*,\s*"dtr-coordinates"\s*:\s*\[([^\]]*)\]\s*,\s*"content"\s*:\s*"([^"]*(?:\\\\.[^"]*)*)"\s*\}""".r

Key change: ([^"]*(?:\\\\.[^"]*)*) instead of ((?:[^"\\\\]|\\\\.)*)).
This avoids catastrophic backtracking by matching non-quotes first, then escaped sequences.

Also add test for large content in JSONFormatTest.scala.
